          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The E06 failure comes from the stated error bounds, and extra precision cannot fix it. I’ll compare the two proposed replacements: integrating logarithms after accounting for nearby zeros, and summing Green contributions from certified zero cells. Each must be costed against direct exclusion on the same region."
            ]
