          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The comparison suggests two useful results. Green bounds formed by summing independent cell maxima can pass only after those same cells already certify direct exclusion. For logarithmic integration, I’m deriving a replacement for E06’s tolerance-sensitive rule that prices root-location error, a certified lower bound for the deflated factor, and integration error separately."
            ]
          },
